# Custom domain for GitHub Pages
#
# 1. Copy this file to CNAME (no extension) at the repo root or in /public
#    so it is emitted into dist/.
# 2. Put your domain on a single line, for example:
#    www.example.com
# 3. In GitHub: Settings → Pages → Custom domain, then add the same host
#    and follow the DNS instructions (A/ALIAS/CNAME records).
#
# Do not commit a live CNAME until the domain is yours.
